messages:
Samir K: incoming from a customer — SSE stream is cutting out after ~60s, they get partial tokens, then client reconnects and gets overlapping output. Customer using our /v1/stream endpoint through an ALB in front of nginx, and sometimes Cloudflare in front of that. Repro attached below.

Samir K: repro (curl):
```
curl -N -H 'Accept: text/event-stream' -H 'Authorization: Bearer <key>' \"https://api.redwood.example.com/v1/stream?model=rw-psi\"
```
They see a few events, then a blank line and connection closed. Client sees WS-like reconnect loop.

Priya V: thanks — can you drop the exact timestamps + any reverse-proxy/nginx/ALB logs? Also do we have response headers from the last chunk?

Samir K: pasted logs from the customer's nginx + ALB TCP logs (sanitized):
```
2025-07-02T14:21:15Z nginx upstream response chunked
2025-07-02T14:22:15Z nginx upstream read timeout, client 10.2.5.8
2025-07-02T14:22:15Z ALB connection closed (idle timeout reached)
```
Headers seen: `Transfer-Encoding: chunked`, `Content-Type: text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, missing `Connection: keep-alive` (proxied away).

Ethan L: ALB idle timeout default is 60s — if there's >60s of inactivity from the downstream connection it will close. SSE often has long gaps unless server emits keepalives. Cloudflare also buffers/resets in some plans (timeouts ~100s) unless you disable buffering/enable stream-friendly route.

Nadia R: couple of quick notes we see frequently:
- If an intermediate proxy buffers the response (nginx with proxy_buffering on, Cloudflare default), the client won't get chunks until the buffer fills or proxy flushes. That looks like 'partial outputs' behavior.
- If the proxy closes the TCP connection because of an idle timeout, the client gets an abrupt close and then reconnects. Duplicate tokens happen when client doesn't dedupe by `id`/message timestamp.

Ethan L: suggested fixes (short):
- Ensure upstream emits regular keepalives/comments (SSE comment lines) every 15s: `: keepalive\n\n` or a small whitespace chunk so proxies see activity.
- For ALB: increase `idle_timeout.timeout_seconds` to something > stream max duration (example 300s). AWS CLI example: `aws elbv2 modify-load-balancer-attributes --load-balancer-arn <arn> --attributes Key=idle_timeout.timeout_seconds,Value=300`
- For nginx (important): disable buffering and extend read timeouts. Example config snippet to put in the proxy block: 
```
proxy_buffering off;
proxy_http_version 1.1;
proxy_set_header Connection '';
proxy_set_header X-Accel-Buffering no;
proxy_read_timeout 3600s;
proxy_send_timeout 3600s;
chunked_transfer_encoding on;
```
- For Cloudflare: if used, prefer a bypass for streaming endpoints (page rule to disable caching and response buffering), or move streaming traffic behind an NLB (TCP passthrough) to avoid HTTP buffering. Cloudflare Workers/Stream product can also be used.
- For Envoy: ensure `stream_idle_timeout` and `idle_timeout` are set appropriately in the `connection_manager` and `route` configs; and `use_remote_address` does not cause early connection termination.

Samir K: customer is on ALB -> nginx -> origin. They reported ALB closed at ~60s and then nginx logged "upstream prematurely closed connection". So ALB closed the downstream while nginx was waiting on origin.

Priya V: action items: 1) Ask customer to add SSE keepalive on their client as a short-term workaround (client will not hang if server reconnects); 2) recommend config changes above; 3) escalate to infra/runtime to consider adding server-side keepalive/heartbeat for our hosted endpoints when streamed responses are idle.

Ethan L: adding some more technical detail for the SR (for eng-runtime):
- Server should include `id:` fields for each SSE event and periodic `:heartbeat` comment lines every 15s when no new tokens emitted. That keeps ALBs and many proxies from deciding the connection is idle.
- Use `Last-Event-ID` / `id` semantics to make client reconnection idempotent — clients should pass `Last-Event-ID` so server can continue without duplicating tokens when possible.
- For hosted infra, we can also send a 1-byte chunk every 20s (`":\n\n"`) if SSE comment is not feasible in some paths.

Nadia R: added nginx troubleshooting checklist to share with customer quickly:
1) Ensure `proxy_buffering off` and `X-Accel-Buffering: no` on the response.
2) `proxy_http_version 1.1` and set `Transfer-Encoding: chunked` preserved.
3) Increase `proxy_read_timeout` > expected stream duration.
4) If ALB present, set ALB idle timeout > longest gap between tokens.
5) If Cloudflare sits in front, instruct them to either disable buffering for that route or use TCP passthrough.

Samir K: customer tried increasing nginx timeouts but couldn't change ALB. They put Cloudflare in front for DDOS protection, which complicated things. They asked whether switching ALB to NLB will fix it.

Ethan L: NLB is TCP-level so it won't buffer/terminate HTTP for idle reasons the same way ALB does, but you'll lose HTTP-level routing and `X-Forwarded-*` behavior unless you implement that in the TCP stack. NLB is a good option if you need transparent passthrough for streaming.

Priya V: I've opened SR-4983 and tagged eng-runtime + infra for follow-up. Customer given the nginx snippet and an example client reconnection pattern (idempotent):
```
// minimal client-side SSE reconnect (browser)
const es = new EventSource(url);
es.onmessage = (e) => {
  const payload = JSON.parse(e.data);
  if (payload.id && processedIds.has(payload.id)) return; // dedupe
  processedIds.add(payload.id);
  handle(payload);
};
es.onerror = () => {
  setTimeout(() => {
    // include last seen id as Last-Event-ID header/query
    connectWithLastId(lastId);
  }, 1000);
};
```
Samir K: customer tried that dedupe approach and it reduced duplicates, but they want us to recommend infra changes so reconnects are rare.

Ethan L: follow-ups for our roadmap:
- Short-term: add server-side SSE heartbeat for hosted streaming endpoints and document ALB/Cloudflare caveats in DevEx guides.
- Medium: add an outbound-edge option (NLB passthrough) for customers who require guaranteed streaming semantics behind third-party proxies.

Priya V: marking this as P1 for support impact — customers hitting duplication + partial output is high friction. I'll follow up with the customer with the nginx config, ALB CLI snippet, and client dedupe example. Also requested a contact at Cloudflare to confirm buffering settings.

infra-bot: SR-4983 assigned to eng-runtime, priority P1, notify: @Ethan L @Nadia R.

Samir K: thanks all — leaving thread open for eng-runtime confirmation on server-side heartbeat and docs update.

Priya V: closing loop — customer will attempt the nginx `proxy_buffering off` + keepalive and report back in 24h. If they can't change ALB, recommend NLB as next step. :thumbsup:
